he course.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:34:22, ahead of Alan ROBB (05:41:26) and Graeme FRASER (05:41:55). Cheryl WINN won the women's race in 07:04:59, followed by Nhlanhla NENE (07:28:39).\n\nCheryl WINN set a new women's down record of 07:04:59, surpassing Isavel ROCHE-KELLY's 07:18:00 from 1980. Cheryl WINN's 07:04:59 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1948 (Bill Savage, 07:13:52).\n\nFrom a field of 4,600 entries, 4,600 runners completed the course for a 100.0% finish rate. The field comprised 4,498 men and 102 women (2.2% female). The average finish time was 09:06:11.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 620 Silver, 3,970 Bronze. 1,499 runners (32.6%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Len SMITH in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1980, the field was 15.6% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 24% of the finishers, with 3,510 seniors (avg 09:03:53) and 1,088 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.0}